    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d85">

                <pb facs="0192" n="946" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v02/pg946"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/4779</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-09-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 18, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2664. Your 2459, September 5. Communicate with Foreign Office and state that in
                    view of removal of firms in United States from black list Department is at loss
                    to understand attitude of French authorities. Letters of Carl Grubnau giving
                    further details going forward by mail.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
